  "operative_text": "Section 1 (C.R.S. 18-12-105(2)(g)): (g) A PERSON WHO WAS AT LEAST TWENTY-ONE YEARS OF AGE AND LEGALLY POSSESSED A HANDGUN UNDER THE LAWS OF THIS STATE AND OF THE UNITED STATES AND THE WEAPON INVOLVED IN THE INCIDENT WAS A HANDGUN. THE AUTHORITY TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN PURSUANT TO THE PROVISIONS OF THIS SUBSECTION (2)(g) IS EQUAL IN ALL RESPECTS TO THE AUTHORITY GRANTED BY A PERMIT TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN AS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 18-12-214. A PERSON WHO CARRIES A CONCEALED HANDGUN PURSUANT TO THE PROVISIONS OF THIS SUBSECTION (2)(g) HAS THE SAME RIGHTS AND IS SUBJECT TO THE SAME LIMITATIONS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 18-12-214 AS APPLY TO A PERSON WHO HOLDS A PERMIT TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN.\nSection 2 (C.R.S. 18-12-105.5(3)(i)): (i) THE PERSON IS AT LEAST TWENTY-ONE YEARS OF AGE AND MAY LEGALLY POSSESS A HANDGUN UNDER THE LAWS OF THIS STATE AND OF THE UNITED STATES AND THE WEAPON INVOLVED IN THE INCIDENT WAS A HANDGUN. THE AUTHORITY TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN PURSUANT TO THE PROVISIONS OF THIS SUBSECTION (3)(i) IS EQUAL IN ALL RESPECTS TO THE AUTHORITY GRANTED BY A PERMIT TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN AS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 18-12-214. A PERSON WHO CARRIES A CONCEALED HANDGUN PURSUANT TO THE PROVISIONS OF THIS SUBSECTION (3)(i) HAS THE SAME RIGHTS AND IS SUBJECT TO THE SAME LIMITATIONS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 18-12-214 AS APPLY TO A PERSON WHO HOLDS A PERMIT TO CARRY A CONCEALED HANDGUN."
}